### Install official Cqrlog (2.5.2 together with MariaDB) to Ubuntu and optionally upgrade it to latest CqrlogImproved

"install_Ubuntu_cqrlog.zip" holds script "install_cqrlog.sh" 
Download, unzip and start it in command console to install Cqrlog without loadng it from Ubuntu's faulty install packet and having MariaDB right away.
Installing is tested several times in plain XUbuntu 26.04, Ubuntu 26.04 and Linux Mint 22.3  but no quarantee is given.

Install will proceed step by step and you have to press enter key to allow next steps to start.
(this way you can halt installation between steps with Ctrl+C if something unexpected happens) 

